# RAG Chatbot Integration Guide

This guide explains how to integrate a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) chatbot with the Physical AI & Humanoid Robotics textbook.

## Architecture Overview

The RAG system consists of three main components:

1. **Document Parser**: Parses the textbook markdown files and extracts content
2. **Vector Store**: Stores document chunks with embeddings for similarity search
3. **Chat Interface**: Frontend component that allows users to ask questions

## Components

### Document Parser (`src/utils/rag/document-parser.js`)
- Parses all textbook markdown files
- Extracts content and metadata
- Splits documents into manageable chunks

### Vector Store (`src/utils/rag/vector-store.js`)
- Stores document embeddings for similarity search
- Implements cosine similarity for finding relevant content
- Provides search functionality

### Embedding Generator (`src/utils/rag/embedding-generator.js`)
- Creates embeddings for text content
- (Currently using mock embeddings - replace with real API in production)

### API Endpoints (`api/rag/`)
- `/api/rag/search`: Search endpoint for querying the textbook
- `/api/rag/index`: Endpoint to re-index documents

### Chat Interface (`src/components/rag/ChatInterface.jsx`)
- React component for the chat interface
- Integrates with the RAG API
- Displays sources for retrieved information

## Setup Instructions

1. Install dependencies:
```bash
npm install react react-dom
```

2. The system will automatically initialize when first accessed, parsing all textbook documents and creating embeddings.

3. To manually re-index documents, call the `/api/rag/index` endpoint.

## Usage

The chat interface can be embedded in any page of the textbook. It will provide answers based on the textbook content with citations to specific sections.

## API Endpoints

### POST /api/rag/search
Search for information in the textbook.

Request body:
```json
{
  "query": "Your question here",
  "topK": 5
}
```

Response:
```json
{
  "query": "Your question here",
  "results": [
    {
      "id": "document-id",
      "content": "Relevant content...",
      "similarity": 0.95,
      "metadata": {
        "source": "module/file.md",
        "title": "Document Title",
        "module": "module-name"
      }
    }
  ],
  "count": 5
}
```

### POST /api/rag/index
Re-index all textbook documents.

Response:
```json
{
  "message": "Document indexing completed successfully",
  "documentCount": 150
}
```

## Customization

To use a real embedding service (like OpenAI), replace the embedding-generator.js implementation with calls to the actual API.

To use a proper vector database (like Pinecone, Weaviate, or Supabase), replace the in-memory vector-store.js implementation.